<form class="form-horizontal">
  <h4>Camera</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Snapshot URL</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xxlarge"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.snapshot_url">
      <span class="help-block">
        A single JPEG frame. OctoPrint fetches this, so 127.0.0.1 is correct.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Frames to average</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.frame_average">
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Finding the camera</h4>
  <div class="alert">
    Nothing is remembered about where the camera is. Every run sweeps the bed
    for it. The X and Y below are where the active T0 nozzle last sat over the
    lens, for information. The Z is where the last focus sweep peaked, and the
    next one starts there.
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Last found X, Y, Z</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.01" class="input-small" readonly
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.camera_x">
      <input type="number" step="0.01" class="input-small" readonly
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.camera_y">
      <input type="number" step="0.01" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.camera_z">
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Bed sweep</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bed_row_mm">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.sweep_step_mm">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.search_z">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.closein_z">
      <span class="help-block">
        Row spacing in Y, step in X, the sweep height and the close-in
        height. At Z90 the camera sees about 75 by 47 mm, so rows 50 mm
        apart cannot miss the toolhead, and the toolhead is wider than the
        field, which is what the close-in needs.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Bore ring span, step (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bed_search_span_mm">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.search_step_mm">
      <span class="help-block">
        How far around the middle of the toolhead the run looks for the bore,
        at the working height.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Heights</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Floor (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.min_z">
      <span class="help-block">
        No move may go below this. The lens sits about 12 mm above the bed on
        the standard mount. Raise this if your mount is taller.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Safe Z (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.safe_z">
      <span class="help-block">Every travel move and every tool change happens at this height.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Focus sweep span, step (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.focus_span_mm">
      <input type="number" step="0.25" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.focus_step_mm">
      <span class="help-block">
        The run sweeps this far above and below the stored Z and stops where
        the bore is sharpest.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Home first</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="checkbox"
             data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.home_first">
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Closed loop</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Probe distance (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.probe_distance">
      <span class="help-block">
        The known move used to measure the pixel scale and the camera rotation.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Backlash take-up (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.backlash_backoff_mm">
      <span class="help-block">
        Every measured position is reached from the same direction, after
        overshooting by this much.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Tolerance (mm), passes</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.001" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.tolerance_mm">
      <input type="number" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.max_passes">
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Bore detector</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Radii (px)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_core_r">
      <input type="number" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_inner_r">
      <input type="number" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_ring_lo">
      <input type="number" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_ring_hi">
      <span class="help-block">
        Ignored centre, dark bore wall, then the bright collar from and to.
        Sized for about 75 px/mm. Check the red circle on the tab.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Minimum score</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_min_score">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_track_score">
      <span class="help-block">
        For a first find, and for a bore already being followed.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Firmware guard</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Toolhead band centre X, Y</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.01" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.nominal_offset_x">
      <input type="number" step="0.01" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.nominal_offset_y">
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Band half width (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.offset_limit_mm">
      <span class="help-block">
        The Snapmaker toolhead throws away an offset outside 26 &plusmn; 1.2 mm
        in X, or 0 &plusmn; 1.2 mm in Y, and resets it to the default. The
        plugin refuses to send such a value.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Also send M500</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="checkbox"
             data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.save_to_eeprom">
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Camera</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Stream URL</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xxlarge"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.stream_url">
      <span class="help-block">An MJPEG stream. The plugin reads about 8 frames a second from it, against one every 0.6 to 0.9 seconds from single snapshots, so a run is far quicker with one. Leave it empty to use snapshots only.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Camera timeout, seconds</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.http_timeout">
      <span class="help-block">How long to wait for a frame before giving up.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Movement</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox"
               data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.home_after">
        Home the printer when a run finishes
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">Leaves the machine in a known place.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Travel feedrate, mm/min</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="100" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.feedrate">
      <span class="help-block">For the long moves between positions.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Fine feedrate, mm/min</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="50" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.fine_feedrate">
      <span class="help-block">For the small corrections that centre a nozzle on the lens.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Z feedrate, mm/min</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="50" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.z_feedrate">
      <span class="help-block">Every descent towards the camera uses this.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Move timeout, seconds</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.move_timeout">
      <span class="help-block">A move that has not finished in this long is treated as a failure.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Homing timeout, seconds</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="10" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.home_timeout">
      <span class="help-block">Homing is slower than a move, so it has its own limit.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Wait after a tool change, seconds</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.tool_settle_s">
      <span class="help-block">The toolhead lifts and drops a nozzle on a tool change. Let it finish.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Wait after a move, seconds</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.settle_s">
      <span class="help-block">Let the frame stop shaking before a picture is taken.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Where to search for the camera</h4>
  <div class="alert alert-error">
    <strong>These four go straight into G1 moves.</strong> A value past your real
    bed drives the toolhead into the frame. They are checked against your printer
    profile when you save and again when you press Calibrate, and a run is refused
    if they do not fit. Keep a margin: the toolhead is wider than the nozzle.
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">X from, millimetres</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bed_x_min">
      <span class="help-block">The area swept while looking for the camera.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">X to, millimetres</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bed_x_max">
      <span class="help-block">The area swept while looking for the camera.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Y from, millimetres</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bed_y_min">
      <span class="help-block">The area swept while looking for the camera.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Y to, millimetres</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bed_y_max">
      <span class="help-block">The area swept while looking for the camera.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Sweep feedrate, mm/min</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="100" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.sweep_feedrate">
      <span class="help-block">The search watches the camera during one continuous move at this speed.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Sweep overrun, seconds</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.sweep_overrun_s">
      <span class="help-block">Extra time allowed past the calculated end of a sweep.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Sweep lag, seconds</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.sweep_lag_s">
      <span class="help-block">How far the picture trails the move, used to place a sighting.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">First search radius, pixels</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="10" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.search_radius_px">
      <span class="help-block">How far from the centre of the frame the first bore may be.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Movement threshold</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.motion_threshold">
      <span class="help-block">How much a pixel must change to count as moved. Raise it if the lighting flickers.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Smallest moved patch</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.05" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.motion_min_blob">
      <span class="help-block">A sighting must be one connected patch at least this fraction of all the movement. It rejects the LED beam and the cable chain.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Nudge, millimetres</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.motion_nudge_mm">
      <span class="help-block">The small move used to tell the toolhead from the background.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Closing in on the camera</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Most steps</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.closein_max_steps">
      <span class="help-block">Give up after this many.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Smallest usable scale, px/mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.closein_min_scale">
      <span class="help-block">Below this the picture is too coarse to steer by.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Smallest usable response</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.05" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.closein_min_response">
      <span class="help-block">How much the picture must answer a move for the step to be trusted.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Close enough, millimetres</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.closein_done_mm">
      <span class="help-block">Stop closing in once the camera is within this.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Largest single step, millimetres</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.closein_max_move_mm">
      <span class="help-block">A cap on any one correction, so a bad reading cannot fling the toolhead.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Focus</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Fine step, millimetres</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.focus_fine_step_mm">
      <span class="help-block">The second, closer sweep uses this step.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Template size, pixels</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="2" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.focus_template_px">
      <span class="help-block">The patch cut out to follow the bore between heights.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Sharpness window, pixels</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="2" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.focus_window_px">
      <span class="help-block">The area measured for sharpness at each height.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Peak ratio</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.05" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.focus_peak_ratio">
      <span class="help-block">The sweep has to fall to this fraction of its best on both sides, or the focus is not inside the sweep and the run stops.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Finding the bore</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Search radius, pixels</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_search_radius_px">
      <span class="help-block">How far from the expected place to look.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Tracking radius, pixels</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.track_search_px">
      <span class="help-block">How far the bore may move between frames and still be followed.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Refine radius, pixels</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.track_lock_px">
      <span class="help-block">How close to the tracked place the detector is allowed to settle.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Tracking confidence</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.05" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.track_min_match">
      <span class="help-block">Below this the template has lost the bore and the detector starts again.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Target X, pixels</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="10" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.target_x_px">
      <span class="help-block">The point in the frame each nozzle is driven onto. The centre by default.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Target Y, pixels</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="10" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.target_y_px">
      <span class="help-block">As above, for Y.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>The pixel to millimetre map</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Attempts</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.map_attempts">
      <span class="help-block">How many times to rebuild a map that does not pass its checks.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Smallest scale, px/mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.map_min_scale">
      <span class="help-block">A map outside the scale band is rejected as untrustworthy.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Largest scale, px/mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.map_max_scale">
      <span class="help-block">As above.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Largest column skew</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.05" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.map_max_cos">
      <span class="help-block">How far from square the two measured directions may be. Near zero is square.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Limits</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Largest correction, millimetres</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.max_correction_mm">
      <span class="help-block">A measurement asking for more than this is refused rather than obeyed.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Raised nozzle check, millimetres</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.active_check_mm">
      <span class="help-block">After a tool change the bore has to appear within this of the target, or the nozzle over the lens was the raised one and the run moves across.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</form>
